---
import iterationsConfig from '../../../versions/iterations.json';
import VersionSwitcher from '../components/VersionSwitcher.astro';
const iterations = iterationsConfig.iterations;
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}favicon.svg`} />
		<link rel="icon" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}favicon.ico`} />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>aito — AI photo editing. Desktop pro. Mobile PWA.</title>
		<style>
			:root {
				--bg: #0a0a0b;
				--fg: #e7e7ea;
				--accent: #ff5b2e;
				--muted: #8a8a93;
				--card: #111113;
			}
			body {
				margin: 0;
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
				font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "SF Pro Display", Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
				line-height: 1.5;
			}
			.container { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; }
			
			.hero {
				text-align: center;
				padding: 6rem 1rem 4rem;
			}
			.hero h1 {
				font-size: 4rem;
				margin: 0 0 1rem;
				letter-spacing: -0.03em;
			}
			.tagline {
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				max-width: 520px;
				margin: 0 auto 2rem;
			}
			.cta-group {
				display: flex;
				gap: 1rem;
				justify-content: center;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}
			.btn {
				display: inline-block;
				padding: 14px 28px;
				border-radius: 8px;
				font-weight: 600;
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: all 0.1s ease;
			}
			.btn.primary {
				background: var(--accent);
				color: #000;
			}
			.btn.secondary {
				background: #222;
				color: #eee;
				border: 1px solid #333;
			}
			.btn.secondary:hover {
				border-color: var(--accent);
			}
			.subtext {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.95rem;
			}

			.features {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
				margin: 4rem 0;
			}
			.feature h3 {
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
				font-size: 1.25rem;
			}
			.feature p {
				color: var(--muted);
				margin: 0;
			}

			.cli-section {
				margin: 5rem 0 3rem;
				padding: 3rem;
				background: #111113;
				border-radius: 12px;
				border: 1px solid #222;
			}
			.cli-lead {
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				max-width: 520px;
			}
			.cli-install {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.5rem;
				margin-top: 1.5rem;
			}
			.install-block h4 {
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				color: var(--muted);
			}
			.install-block pre {
				background: #0a0a0b;
				padding: 12px 16px;
				border-radius: 6px;
				margin: 0;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}
			.cli-note {
				margin-top: 1.5rem;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}

			.screenshots {
				margin: 4rem 0;
			}
			.screenshot-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(420px, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
			}
			.screenshot img {
				width: 100%;
				border-radius: 8px;
				border: 1px solid #222;
				box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
			}
			.screenshot .caption {
				margin-top: 0.75rem;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				text-align: center;
			}

			.screenshot-placeholder {
				width: 100%;
				aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
				background: linear-gradient(145deg, #111113 0%, #0a0a0b 100%);
				border: 1px solid #222;
				border-radius: 8px;
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				color: #555;
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				font-family: monospace;
			}

			.tools {
				margin: 4rem 0 3rem;
			}
			.tool-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.75rem 2rem;
			}
			.tool h4 {
				margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
				font-size: 1rem;
				color: #fff;
			}
			.tool p {
				margin: 0;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.92rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			footer {
				text-align: center;
				padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="container">
			<header class="hero">
				<h1>aito</h1>
				<p class="tagline">
					AI photo editing, built for the way you actually work.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-group">
					<a href="/aito/" class="btn primary">
						Open aito
					</a>
					<a href="#live-canvas" class="btn secondary">
						Get Live Canvas CLI
					</a>
					<a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}hub/`} class="btn secondary">
						Hub &amp; iterations
					</a>
				</div>
				<p class="subtext">
					Real-time Grok commands. Live camera tethering. Proper film emulation.<br>
					<strong>Works beautifully on desktop and as a mobile PWA.</strong>
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="features">
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Live Tethering</h3>
					<p>Connect directly to local cameras and devices. Real-time preview straight into the editor.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>AI That Actually Helps</h3>
					<p>Grok-powered commands. Describe the look you want — adjustments, LUTs, and masking happen instantly.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Production-Grade Tools</h3>
					<p>Masked corrections, brush refinement, film emulation LUTs, and a proper bake history.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="screenshots">
				<h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">See it in action</h2>
				<div class="screenshot-grid">
					<div class="screenshot">
						<img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}screenshots/desktop-hero.jpg`} alt="aito desktop editor with 3-column layout: main before/after slider, tools panel, and right inspector showing live tether controls + EXIF metadata" />
						<p class="caption">Desktop pro layout — full 3-column with tether inspector and EXIF on the right</p>
					</div>
					<div class="screenshot">
						<img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}screenshots/mobile-pwa.jpg`} alt="aito running as mobile PWA on iPhone with bottom action bar and open AI command sheet" />
						<p class="caption">Mobile PWA — clean image-first experience with bottom sheets for AI, tools, and live tether</p>
					</div>
					<div class="screenshot">
						<img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}screenshots/lut-desktop.jpg`} alt="aito LUT film emulation controls open in the right panel with strong cinematic grade on landscape" />
						<p class="caption">Film emulation LUTs with live preview across VSCO, Kodak, Fuji and cinema looks</p>
					</div>
					<div class="screenshot">
						<img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}screenshots/brush-refine.jpg`} alt="aito brush refinement active on a subject mask with hardness controls visible" />
						<p class="caption">Precise brush refinement on AI-generated masks</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="tools">
				<h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Key tools</h2>
				<div class="tool-grid">
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>AI Prompt Bar</h4>
						<p>Command the editor in plain language. Grok sees the current image + bake graph and returns structured edits (adjustments, LUT choice, mask prompt, intensity). Changes land as nodes in the non-destructive history.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>Live Tethering</h4>
						<p>Bidirectional WebSocket to a local companion (exact pattern used in the fornevercollective live lab tools). Camera frames stream in real time; send ISO, shutter, and capture commands from the browser. The glowing “LIVE VIEW” badge in the top bar is the single source of truth while tethered — click it to open controls.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>Film Emulation LUTs</h4>
						<p>Curated library across VSCO, Kodak (Portra 400/160, 2383), Fuji (Superia, 3510), cinema (Teal &amp; Orange, Bleach Bypass), and lens looks. Load your own .cube or Hald CLUT files. Per-layer intensity slider with instant preview.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>Masked Corrections</h4>
						<p>SAM-powered subject / background masks drive the full adjustment stack: exposure, contrast, saturation, temperature, tint, clarity, vignette, sharpen, and lutIntensity. Every control respects the active mask and scope toggles.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>Brush Refinement</h4>
						<p>Soft, pressure-sensitive brush with adjustable hardness. Paint directly on the mask to add or remove areas. Brush strokes are first-class nodes in the bake tree — fully revisable.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tool">
						<h4>Hatch Export &amp; Bake Tree</h4>
						<p>Export Subject only, Background only, or full composite with the diagnostic hatch overlay for easy keying in Resolve or Photoshop. Every AI command and brush stroke is recorded as a BakeNode for versioning and incremental re-evaluation.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="live-canvas" class="cli-section">
				<h2>Live Canvas</h2>
				<p class="cli-lead">
					The local CLI companion for aito.<br>
					Real-time camera tethering, advanced LUT pipelines, and the tools you reach for on set.
				</p>

				<div class="cli-install">
					<div class="install-block">
						<h4>npm</h4>
						<pre><code>npm install -g @fornevercollective/live-canvas</code></pre>
					</div>
					<div class="install-block">
						<h4>Homebrew</h4>
						<pre><code>brew install fornevercollective/tap/live-canvas</code></pre>
					</div>
					<div class="install-block">
						<h4>Download</h4>
						<a href="https://github.com/fornevercollective/aito/releases/latest" class="btn">macOS • Linux • Windows</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<p class="cli-note">
					<a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}versions/living-canvas/`}>Architecture &amp; research →</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<footer>
				<p>
					Open source • <a href="https://github.com/fornevercollective/aito">GitHub</a> • <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}hub/`}>Hub</a> • <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}brand/`}>Brand</a> • <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}pricing/`}>Pricing</a> • <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}license/`}>License</a>
				</p>
				<p style="margin-top:0.6rem; font-size:0.82rem; color:#555;">
					Install aito as a PWA on iOS or Android for the full mobile experience.
				</p>
			</footer>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>